1
00:00:01,893 --> 00:00:20,975
[SPEAKER_00]: So, here's another short sutta excerpt from Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gautama Gaut

2
00:00:22,366 --> 00:00:41,459
[SPEAKER_00]: So, one thing, because when developed and cultivated, leads to great anxiety, leads to great welfare, leads to great security from bondage, leads to mindfulness and awareness, leads to acquisition of knowledge and vision, and leads to pleasant dwelling here and now, leads to realization of the fruit of knowledge and liberation.

3
00:00:41,759 --> 00:00:42,680
[SPEAKER_00]: Which one thing?

4
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:44,421
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of the body.

5
00:00:45,788 --> 00:00:52,091
[SPEAKER_00]: This because is the one thing that which, when developed and cultivated, leads to great anxiety, great welfare, great security from bondage, and so on.

6
00:00:53,291 --> 00:01:00,714
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh... you might wonder here, why it says, eh... great anxiety, great concern.

7
00:01:01,835 --> 00:01:01,975
[SPEAKER_00]: Eh...

8
00:01:04,557 --> 00:01:32,506
[SPEAKER_00]: It refers to when you start recognizing kind of the necessary preconditions, which is the certain recognition of the inevitability of suffering, for example, and then that the fact that you are not... well, you are liable, you're subjected to sickness, aging and death, all these things that can befall one's body,

9
00:01:33,235 --> 00:01:37,677
[SPEAKER_00]: They will... they would affect and sometimes even undermine your own life.

10
00:01:37,837 --> 00:01:40,718
[SPEAKER_00]: You're completely... you remain completely liable to those things.

11
00:01:41,298 --> 00:01:44,959
[SPEAKER_00]: So, most people live their life completely ignoring that.

12
00:01:45,039 --> 00:01:50,901
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why when the Buddha went out of his palace, he referred to things he'd seen as divine messengers.

13
00:01:51,241 --> 00:02:00,805
[SPEAKER_00]: They were basically conveying a message of a certain reality that awaits every human, yet most of the people managed to sort of spend their life pretty much

14
00:02:02,245 --> 00:02:04,347
[SPEAKER_00]: covering, covering the very reality up.

15
00:02:05,247 --> 00:02:25,138
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the first thing is going to happen, if you start practicing mindfulness of the body correctly, is you're going to experience anxiety, because suddenly you're rediscovering that the fact that you are you're out there in the world, you're liable to these things, you're not in control,

16
00:02:26,507 --> 00:02:31,448
[SPEAKER_00]: And, like the circumstances, elements, you're fully subjected to it.

17
00:02:31,708 --> 00:02:40,950
[SPEAKER_00]: You're like, as the Buddha said, you're like a flayed cow that's being consumed by... if it leans on the wall for support, it gets eaten by the insects that are on the wall.

18
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:45,591
[SPEAKER_00]: If it lays down for support, it gets eaten by the insects that are living on the ground.

19
00:02:45,671 --> 00:02:47,591
[SPEAKER_00]: If it stands, the ones that live in the air, and so on.

20
00:02:48,111 --> 00:02:55,233
[SPEAKER_00]: So, attending to the... maintaining that mindfulness of the body correctly, the recollectiveness of the...

21
00:02:56,935 --> 00:03:04,113
[SPEAKER_00]: It's pretty much of the nature of the body, which is the nature of that being subjected to illness, being subjected to things that are...

22
00:03:05,541 --> 00:03:07,083
[SPEAKER_00]: That you cannot possibly foresee.

23
00:03:07,583 --> 00:03:16,271
[SPEAKER_00]: So, having that on the back of your mind, as a certain context that you cultivate, will have to result in anxiety.

24
00:03:16,852 --> 00:03:17,693
[SPEAKER_00]: Initially, at least.

25
00:03:17,813 --> 00:03:21,657
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the anxiety, it's a symptom of that cover-up.

26
00:03:21,917 --> 00:03:28,924
[SPEAKER_00]: If you haven't been covering a certain reality up, in regard to things you are liable to, you wouldn't be anxious about it.

27
00:03:30,047 --> 00:03:44,235
[SPEAKER_00]: So, anxiety is that... is that sort of a crack in that plaster that you have applied on the... on the certain aspects of existence that you refuse to admit to yourself, because they are far too unpleasant.

28
00:03:45,756 --> 00:03:58,184
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in this... in this sutta, in particular, it says that if you were to cultivate then that mindfulness properly, it will lead to... to great anxiety, more like a great concern.

29
00:03:59,429 --> 00:04:06,274
[SPEAKER_00]: A recognition of great concern, which is pretty much a necessary step for you to look for the way out.

30
00:04:06,574 --> 00:04:15,600
[SPEAKER_00]: If you don't, if you don't experience that concern, or as the Buddha would say, or even try and invoke in monks that got complacent and lazy, a sense of urgency.

31
00:04:16,641 --> 00:04:19,543
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you need to recognize that time might be short,

32
00:04:20,992 --> 00:04:40,027
[SPEAKER_00]: Your entire life, the way you know it, things that are dear to you, things that are not dear to you, everything, your preferences, your sense desires, things that you go through on a daily basis, all of that is there, undermined by the nature of the body that you are not in control of.

33
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:49,995
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you could think of it in terms of, like, you're closed in a vehicle, in a car, that it's running down the hill, and there are no brakes.

34
00:04:51,306 --> 00:04:56,408
[SPEAKER_00]: Or maybe brakes work like in a limited manner, let's say like that, to be a bit more accurate.

35
00:04:57,368 --> 00:05:01,129
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you can slow down or not, but you cannot completely stop.

36
00:05:01,209 --> 00:05:03,210
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible.

37
00:05:04,811 --> 00:05:11,953
[SPEAKER_00]: You can steer to the left, you can steer to the right, you can choose the direction, but what do you think... one thing you cannot do is stop going downhill.

38
00:05:13,293 --> 00:05:20,176
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's pretty much the human existence, the life we are kind of living and leading.

39
00:05:21,281 --> 00:05:23,243
[SPEAKER_00]: It's all heading in that certain direction.

40
00:05:24,224 --> 00:05:25,404
[SPEAKER_00]: And there's nothing you can do about it.

41
00:05:25,685 --> 00:05:35,372
[SPEAKER_00]: But, most of the people, and the minds that are not untrained, they are unable to bear that recognition, that you are heading downhill.

42
00:05:36,013 --> 00:05:41,838
[SPEAKER_00]: One way or the other, it doesn't matter how good, how great your life might be, death is inevitable.

43
00:05:43,099 --> 00:05:44,039
[SPEAKER_00]: Aging is inevitable.

44
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,240
[SPEAKER_00]: Sickness is inevitable.

45
00:05:45,581 --> 00:05:48,263
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you were to not lose the sight of this context,

46
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:52,740
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, there are many things, then, that you would not do in this life.

47
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:57,901
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you would not take for granted your own senses, the pleasure you get from your own senses.

48
00:05:57,921 --> 00:06:00,201
[SPEAKER_00]: You would not take for granted irritation and ill-will.

49
00:06:00,221 --> 00:06:01,342
[SPEAKER_00]: You wouldn't be acting out of it.

50
00:06:01,782 --> 00:06:05,402
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it was said in... or maybe it was in the Buddha, but it was in the Dhammapada.

51
00:06:07,263 --> 00:06:12,404
[SPEAKER_00]: It was said that people who quarrel and bear grudges...

52
00:06:12,424 --> 00:06:13,484
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm kind of paraphrasing.

53
00:06:14,044 --> 00:06:16,985
[SPEAKER_00]: People who quarrel and bear grudges are the ones that forget.

54
00:06:18,457 --> 00:06:20,459
[SPEAKER_00]: That in this world we are all condemned to die.

55
00:06:20,759 --> 00:06:31,546
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, if you were to not forget the ultimate direction that that vehicle, car, is heading, you just... it would be impossible for you to bear a grudge.

56
00:06:31,606 --> 00:06:46,957
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whenever you find yourself bearing grudges or ill-will or chasing sensuality, that can only be done on a basis of ignoring the fact that you are liable to death.

57
00:06:48,294 --> 00:06:49,454
[SPEAKER_00]: And the death is inevitable.

58
00:06:49,934 --> 00:07:01,197
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why one of the chief of the mindfulness that you can practice is mindfulness of death, which is closely, obviously, it's inseparable from mindfulness of the body.

59
00:07:01,897 --> 00:07:04,358
[SPEAKER_00]: It results in the same recognitions.

60
00:07:04,378 --> 00:07:10,759
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's how it would lead to great anxiety, the useful anxiety, the anxiety that can then reveal the cover-up.

61
00:07:12,719 --> 00:07:14,820
[SPEAKER_00]: And because of that, you seek your own welfare.

62
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:19,344
[SPEAKER_00]: If you keep doing it, you'll stop feeling anxious, because you stop covering it up.

63
00:07:20,145 --> 00:07:22,046
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, it will lead to your great welfare.

64
00:07:23,267 --> 00:07:27,209
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, furthermore, it will lead to the security from bondage.

65
00:07:27,229 --> 00:07:27,469
[SPEAKER_00]: Eh...

66
00:07:27,489 --> 00:07:36,094
[SPEAKER_00]: In this particular meaning is security from bondage, basically, things that bind you, are things that you find dear and pleasing to you.

67
00:07:36,654 --> 00:07:39,536
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they don't direct... they don't bind you directly, so to speak.

68
00:07:39,576 --> 00:07:42,358
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not the fault of the things that you're bound by them.

69
00:07:43,471 --> 00:07:47,214
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the fault of you valuing the pleasure that you get through those things.

70
00:07:47,294 --> 00:07:49,375
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, those things become your bond.

71
00:07:51,297 --> 00:07:54,719
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you were to uproot the value of pleasure, you have severed the bond.

72
00:07:56,100 --> 00:08:02,505
[SPEAKER_00]: And you would do that if you practice... if you maintain that recollectedness of the context of your body correctly.

73
00:08:02,525 --> 00:08:07,749
[SPEAKER_00]: And when I say the body, I don't mean sensations of your body and and so on that you might be attending to.

74
00:08:07,769 --> 00:08:10,311
[SPEAKER_00]: It means context of the body, the nature of the body.

75
00:08:10,351 --> 00:08:11,552
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the body liable to?

76
00:08:11,592 --> 00:08:13,073
[SPEAKER_00]: What are the characteristics of the body?

77
00:08:13,853 --> 00:08:17,856
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the... what are the implications of having body?

78
00:08:19,238 --> 00:08:34,190
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's liability to sickness, aging and death, liability to elements, having to endure them, liability to hot, cold, abusive experiences, words that are unpleasant to hear.

79
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:38,033
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, being devoured by the senses and pressured by the senses.

80
00:08:38,153 --> 00:08:39,815
[SPEAKER_00]: That is the nature of the body.

81
00:08:40,988 --> 00:08:48,552
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when we say mindfulness of the body or recollectiveness of the body, that is what you must keep recollected and be mindful of.

82
00:08:48,632 --> 00:08:52,174
[SPEAKER_00]: Not, I'm touching my feeling, feeling, I'm feeling things in my back.

83
00:08:52,214 --> 00:08:56,896
[SPEAKER_00]: None of that actually stands for the body, nor is it even a recollectiveness of the body.

84
00:08:56,936 --> 00:09:03,180
[SPEAKER_00]: Just literally focusing on the tactile aspects of your present experience as a whole.

85
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:07,482
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why often people misconstrue the whole idea of sensations, that somehow they're feeling.

86
00:09:07,502 --> 00:09:07,902
[SPEAKER_00]: They're not.

87
00:09:08,397 --> 00:09:15,422
[SPEAKER_00]: Sensations that you observe throughout your body are basically tactile, like your attention following the tactile directions.

88
00:09:15,522 --> 00:09:15,922
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

89
00:09:16,603 --> 00:09:19,244
[SPEAKER_00]: So, on account of touch, you somehow can become an arahant.

90
00:09:19,284 --> 00:09:19,825
[SPEAKER_00]: Impossible.

91
00:09:20,845 --> 00:09:24,008
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness of the body means body as a unit, body as a whole.

92
00:09:24,248 --> 00:09:30,012
[SPEAKER_00]: Things that, regardless of sight, sound, smell, taste, touch, things that you are liable to.

93
00:09:31,353 --> 00:09:34,735
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is sickness, aging, death, non-control, impermanence, all of that.

94
00:09:36,707 --> 00:10:02,553
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why, by severing that bondage, it would lead to that establishment of composure, of samādhi, through that mindfulness and awareness, which then leads to, like, thoroughly, completely uncovering anything you've been covering up, freeing yourself from the contradictions of desires, ill-will and so on, leads to the acquisition of knowledge and vision, which leads to pleasant abiding right here, right now.

95
00:10:02,793 --> 00:10:05,074
[SPEAKER_00]: As in, pleasant abiding means ease.

96
00:10:06,133 --> 00:10:10,615
[SPEAKER_00]: You're free from bondage, free from pressure, free from anxiety.

97
00:10:10,635 --> 00:10:12,516
[SPEAKER_00]: It means you're at ease.

98
00:10:12,636 --> 00:10:14,356
[SPEAKER_00]: You have laid down the burden.

99
00:10:14,397 --> 00:10:17,578
[SPEAKER_00]: You're completely free.

100
00:10:19,699 --> 00:10:23,780
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is exactly what leads then to realization of the fruit of that knowledge and liberation.

101
00:10:23,921 --> 00:10:26,121
[SPEAKER_00]: Arahantship.

102
00:10:26,402 --> 00:10:31,984
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in that sense, if you practice mindfulness of the body, and also you can see how it would then result in knowledge.

103
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,583
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's not just a random technique that you're observing your body, how it moves or how it sits.

104
00:10:38,323 --> 00:10:38,443
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

105
00:10:38,544 --> 00:10:46,889
[SPEAKER_00]: You're dwelling on the aspects of the body that kind of, well, certainly direct and they signify your whole life.

106
00:10:47,950 --> 00:10:52,093
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you know, if you're ignoring that you're liable to sickness, aging and death,

107
00:10:53,012 --> 00:10:55,954
[SPEAKER_00]: That is your context, like ignoring the certain truths.

108
00:10:56,474 --> 00:11:05,279
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why you would commit to various things in life, be bound by them, chase them, obviously implying that they will last forever, ignoring the fact that they can't.

109
00:11:05,559 --> 00:11:09,421
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's a direct result of you not having the proper context of your body.

110
00:11:10,642 --> 00:11:19,707
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if on the other hand, you were to change, change the background of that context and start dwelling on things that are

111
00:11:22,131 --> 00:11:27,675
[SPEAKER_00]: that the body is liable to, then that will have to then shape your other decisions on a smaller scale.

112
00:11:28,415 --> 00:11:33,419
[SPEAKER_00]: You will not possibly make careless choices and decisions out of the careful context.

113
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,219
[SPEAKER_00]: It's impossible.

114
00:11:34,679 --> 00:11:36,421
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why context is all.

115
00:11:36,721 --> 00:11:39,142
[SPEAKER_00]: Mindfulness is fundamentally what context is.

116
00:11:39,202 --> 00:11:42,505
[SPEAKER_00]: Practicing mindfulness is practicing the clarification of the context.

117
00:11:42,985 --> 00:11:45,226
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it's... you can't have too much of that.

118
00:11:45,306 --> 00:11:50,607
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't be too clear about the context that you are liable to, the context of your existence.

119
00:11:51,127 --> 00:12:01,030
[SPEAKER_00]: You can have too much focusing, you can have too much of non-focusing, be too slack, but you cannot have too much of clarity in regard to the context of your body.

120
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:01,891
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just impossible.

121
00:12:03,471 --> 00:12:07,612
[SPEAKER_00]: And the more... the clearer you are, the more of the knowledge and recognition gets established.

122
00:12:07,672 --> 00:12:10,213
[SPEAKER_00]: And the more of the proper samādhi you develop,

123
00:12:11,174 --> 00:12:19,321
[SPEAKER_00]: Because now your samādhi is unshakable, because the recognition of what the nature of the body is, you cannot forget.

124
00:12:19,782 --> 00:12:21,143
[SPEAKER_00]: Because how could you forget?

125
00:12:21,223 --> 00:12:26,088
[SPEAKER_00]: Because any experience you have is within these five senses.

126
00:12:26,248 --> 00:12:28,190
[SPEAKER_00]: Within these five senses and the mind, of course.

127
00:12:28,990 --> 00:12:31,352
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's within the body, strictly speaking.

128
00:12:31,393 --> 00:12:32,233
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what Buddha meant.

129
00:12:32,534 --> 00:12:34,155
[SPEAKER_00]: The body is the universe for you.

130
00:12:34,575 --> 00:12:37,158
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing outside that you could perceive or even conceive.

131
00:12:37,995 --> 00:12:41,718
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the extent of the universe is the extent of the body.

132
00:12:41,918 --> 00:12:46,642
[SPEAKER_00]: The entire universe is contained in this body less than two meters tall, as the Buddha said it.

133
00:12:48,723 --> 00:13:06,977
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you were to clarify the context of that universe, the certain characteristics of impermanence, characteristics of that lack of satisfaction, you would not be able to basically maintain all the things that depend upon those characteristics not being clarified.

134
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:17,012
[SPEAKER_00]: Such is sensuality, ill-will, anger, carelessness, indolence and pretty much everything else that's by definition unwholesome.

